/*
 * Detection basis: upload-intent egress (T1041/T1573-analog). SINGLE-EVENT signal:
 * a curl process launched by a script/interpreter whose command line carries upload
 * arguments. It proves upload INTENT by the invoking interpreter - never a
 * successful send. No archive name, IP, port or hostname is required.
 * Network ownership: E1<->E3 by process.entity_id is a separate ledger/verifier
 * join (S6, GAP when the E3 lacks attribution); a host/time E1-E3 join is NOT used,
 * because it would risk attributing another process' connection to this curl.
 * Transfer success: the sink receipt + manifest-receipt equality.
 */
process where
  winlog.event_id : "1"
  and winlog.channel : "Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational"
  and process.name : "curl.exe"
  and process.parent.name : ("powershell.exe", "cmd.exe", "wscript.exe", "cscript.exe")
  and process.command_line : ("*-T *", "*--upload-file*", "*-F *", "*--form*", "*--data-binary*", "*-d *")